\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RpppSubjSubst
\item[* relevant examples:] He (seems) against the analysis
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] preppproptoformula
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) RC\_pppSubst
\item[* date of creation:] 8-MAR-1989
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] Dutch RAdjSubstitution3
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 9/3/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders.\\
Removed conditions on deixis of PREPPFORMULA, since they do not matter (a prop
will assume the superdeixis of the verb (sentence) it is substituted into).
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] Substitution of subject NPs. Needed because in Spanish some 
structures do not take a subject in the main clause (the Spanish variant of 
`Hij bleek een dokter' does not exist; there only is `Het bleek dat hij een 
dokter is')
